# ---- generated and captured output ----
#
# Every directory below is written by a tool and is reproducible by re-running
# it: qa.mjs, shot.mjs, test-variety.mjs, scatter-census.mjs, test-parity.mjs and
# demo-capture.mjs. The browser tools additionally drop multi-hundred-megabyte
# Chrome profiles into theirs. None of it is repository content.
#
# ref-images/ and dbg-images/ are the exception to the "reproducible" half and
# not to the rule: they are hand-captured art-direction and debugging frames,
# local reference material that no tool can regenerate. They are still not
# repository content. Keep your own backup - nothing here will restore them.
#
# THESE ARE WHOLE-DIRECTORY RULES ON PURPOSE. No per-file exceptions, no
# per-extension patterns. The arrangement this replaced carried forty lines of
# `!` re-includes for milestone reports, and it only worked because the parent
# directory itself was left un-excluded - exclude the directory and no `!` below
# it can bring anything back, which is a trap nobody remembers at the moment
# they add the rule. If a report becomes a reference someone will diff against
# later, copy it OUT of these directories; do not punch a hole in the rule.
census-output/
dbg-images/
demo-output/
parity-output/
qa-output/
ref-images/
shot-output/
shot-output-before/
variety-output/

# ---- local working notes ----
#
# NOTES_* are working documents - bug lists, biome briefs, session handoffs -
# that belong to whoever is doing the work, not to the repository. They get
# rewritten and deleted between sessions, so NOTHING IN THE TREE MAY CITE ONE BY
# NAME: a comment pointing at a file no clone has is exactly the dead-reference
# bug this project keeps repeating. State the finding at the site that depends
# on it instead. (STATUS.md was the same kind of document and was deleted in
# f32d5a4; its 35 citations came out with this rule.)
NOTES_*

# ---- dependencies ----
#
# There are no runtime dependencies and there must never be any (see CLAUDE.md),
# but the tooling still runs under node, so keep an accidental install out.
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# ---- agent and editor state ----
#
# .claude/ holds per-machine Claude Code state (settings.local.json, task locks).
# It was excluded only by `.git/info/exclude`, which is PER-CLONE and does not
# travel: the rule has to live here or the next clone offers the directory up.
.claude/

# ---- editor and OS noise ----
.DS_Store
*.log
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
